<title>USA: U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights -- USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights -- USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA wheat export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Net sales of 359,500 metric tons (MT) were 2 percent above the previous week and 27 percent over the 4-week average.  The major buyers were Pakistan (180,000 MT), Mexico (57,900 MT), Japan (34,700 MT), and Ecuador (21,000 MT).</p>
<p>Exports of 186,500 MT--a marketing-year low--were 37 percentbelow the week earlier and 56 percent under the 4-week average. The primary destinations were Egypt (48,500 MT), South Korea (47,000 MT), Taiwan (42,000 MT), and Mexico (25,200 MT).</p>
</text>
